1
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,200
An idea is the most resilient parasite.
A trace of it always remains.

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:11,400
Once an idea has taken hold of the brain,
it's almost impossible to eradicate.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,600
Cobb, what exactly are you doing
in my subconscious?

4
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:19,800
Inception. We plant an idea
so deep it feels like their own.

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:24,000
Not stealing — planting.
You think it can actually be done?

6
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:28,200
I've done it before.
Once, a long time ago.

7
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,500
[traffic noise, rain on glass]
Your totem. What is it?

8
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:36,700
A top. When it keeps spinning,
I know I'm still in a dream.

9
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:41,000
When it falls, I'm awake.
That's all the certainty I need.

10
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:45,200
We go three levels deep.
Dream within a dream within a dream.

11
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:49,400
Robert Fischer. His father's empire.
We break it before he inherits it.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,700
The subconscious is always hostile
to an intruder. He'll have trained defenses.

13
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:58,000
Projections. His mind will
send them after us like a military unit.

14
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,200
[gunfire in the distance]
Ariadne. Design the maze.

15
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:06,400
The maze can't double back on itself.
His subconscious will notice.

16
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,700
Sixty seconds of real time
becomes ten minutes down here.

17
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:15,000
At the second level, five hours.
Third level: days become weeks.

18
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:19,200
<i>And below that? Limbo.</i>
<i>Unconstructed dream space.</i>

19
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:23,400
<i>Raw infinite subconscious.</i>
<i>Time moves differently there. Years feel like decades.</i>

20
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,700
You've been to Limbo?
How did you get out?

21
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:32,000
I had to let go of everything
I thought I knew was real.

22
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:36,200
Mal — she was my wife.
She died because of something I did.

23
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:40,500
She couldn't tell the difference
between the dream world and reality anymore.

24
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:44,700
I planted an idea in her mind.
That her world wasn't real.

25
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:49,000
That was inception. The only way back
was to die... and wake up.

26
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:53,200
But she woke up and kept believing it.
She thought reality was still the dream.

27
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:57,400
She jumped from the window.
She believed she'd wake up again.

28
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,700
[tense orchestral swell]
The kick. That's how we wake each other.

29
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:06,000
A sudden physical jolt.
We need synchronized kicks at every level.

30
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:10,200
Arthur handles zero gravity.
Eames takes the third level.

31
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:14,400
Yusuf drives. The van hits the bridge rail —
that's the first kick.

32
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,700
I need five minutes alone with Fischer.
To show him the safe. His father's secret.

33
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:23,000
What's in the safe doesn't matter.
What matters is what he believes is in there.

34
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:27,200
The pinwheel. His father kept it by his bed.
Fischer used to make them as a child.

35
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:31,500
That's the emotional core.
Disappointment. That his father loved him.

36
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:35,700
Robert, I'm not ashamed of you.
I was disappointed... in myself.

37
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:40,000
[Fischer weeping softly]
He's never going to hear those words for real.

38
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:44,200
But in the dream, he believes it.
That's the idea. That's the inception.

39
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:48,500
Dissolve the corporation.
That's the thought we plant.

40
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:52,700
Not as a command. As his own idea,
born from his own grief.

41
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:57,000
Cobb, she's not real. Mal.
She's a projection of your guilt.

42
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:01,200
I know. But knowing isn't the same
as letting go. She feels real to me.

43
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:05,400
Every time I close my eyes
I see her face. My children's faces.

44
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,700
I can't picture them anymore.
Only with their backs turned.

45
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:14,000
This job gets me home.
One clear shot to get back to my children.

46
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:18,200
The top is spinning on the table.
Everyone's watching it.

47
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:22,400
Cobb doesn't watch it. He doesn't wait
for it to fall. He walks away.

48
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,700
His children. He runs to them.
He can finally see their faces.

49
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:31,000
[soft orchestral music]
The top wobbles. Just slightly.

50
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:35,200
But we never see it fall.
Is he dreaming? Is he awake?
That's the point.
